WEBVTT

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.830
What's wrong?

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.030
Look...

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.490
What is that?!

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:30.750
<i>In Japan, there are seven young 
men and women of worldwide renown</i>

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.890
<i>whose talents are so remarkable</i>

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>that one would not believe 
they are in high school.</i>

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:39.620
<i>Out of respect and awe for their abilities,</i>

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.090
<i>people call them "high school prodigies."</i>

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.530
<i>A girl with intelligence several 
centuries ahead of her time,</i>

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.940
<i>whom espionage agents around the world 
constantly have their eye on...</i>

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.040
<i>Ringo-chan!</i>

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:12.670
What is it, Bearabbit?

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.460
<i>You need to bear toward Earth soon,</i>

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:18.300
<i>or you'll be late for your appointment!</i>

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.160
Oh, right.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.910
<i>Her name is Ohoshi Ringo.</i>

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:27.270
<b>Ohoshi Ringo</b>

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.270
<i>Despite being in high school, 
she's the world's top inventor.</i>

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.270
<b>The World's Top</b>

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.270
<b>Inventor</b>

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.900
<i>A hero who, with sword in hand,</i>

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:42.030
<i>races through war zones
while bullets fly around her...</i>

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.000
It is a samurai's right to strike.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.980
<i>Her name is Ichijo Aoi.</i>

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:59.220
<b>Ichijo Aoi</b>

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.220
<i>Despite being in high school,
she is the world's top swordsman.</i>

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.220
<b>The World's Top</b>

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.220
<b>Swordsman</b>

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:13.730
<i>Her medical talents make
the human lifespan itself a flimsy concept.</i>

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:21.990
The procedure is complete.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.840
<i>Her name is Kanzaki Keine.</i>

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:32.160
<b>Kanzaki Keine</b>

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.160
<b>The World's Top</b>

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.160
<i>Despite being in high school, 
she is the world's top doctor.</i>

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.160
<b>Doctor</b>

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.580
<i>The devil of the financial world,</i>

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.430
<i>who has a hand in roughly 30 percent of
all monetary transactions across the globe...</i>

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:50.100
What's up?

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.850
What? The loan's in the bag?

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.880
With an additional ten billion yen?

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.580
Okay, great.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.140
Everything's going just as I planned.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.450
<i>His name is Sanada Masato.</i>

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:04.860
<b>Sanada Masato</b>

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.860
<i>Despite being in high school,
he is the world's top entrepreneur.</i>

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.860
<b>The World's Top</b>

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.860
<b>Entrepreneur</b>

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.180
<i>Clairvoyance, telekinesis, levitation:</i>

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.740
<i>this illusionist has mastered every art.</i>

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.210
It's showtime!

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.010
Did you see? This is...

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.440
my magic!

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.870
<i>His name is Prince Akatsuki.</i>

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.360
<b>Prince Akatsuki</b>

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.360
<i>Despite being in high school, 
he is the world's top magician.</i>

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.360
<b>The World's Top</b>

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.360
<b>Magician</b>

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.500
<i>A descendant of the ninja Sarutobi Sasuke,</i>

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.910
<i>with an unmatched talent for espionage...</i>

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.160
I see a scoop!

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.010
Nin, nin!

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.280
<i>Her name is Sarutobi Shinobu.</i>

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.510
<b>Sarutobi Shinobu</b>

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.510
<i>Despite being in high school, 
she is the world's top journalist.</i>

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.510
<b>The World's Top</b>

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.510
<b>Journalist</b>

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.770
<i>The young man who was 
elected Prime Minister</i>

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:22.070
<i>in Japan's first direct popular vote 
for the head of government...</i>

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.880
As a result of the general election,

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.660
I am once again granted the esteemed 
position of Prime Minister.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.230
Henceforth...

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.820
<i>His name is Mikogami Tsukasa.</i>

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:37.160
<b>Mikogami Tsukasa</b>

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:37.160
<i>Despite being in high school,
he is the world's top politician.</i>

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:37.160
<b>The World's Top</b>

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.160
<b>Politician</b>

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.170
<i>A few days later,</i>

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:47.670
<i>somewhere far, far from here, 
the fates of these seven young people</i>

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:51.080
<i>would come together in
the beginning of a new story...</i>

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:02.690
<b>High School Prodigies Have
Arrived in Another World!</b>

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.690
You've awakened? Thank goodness!

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.570
Am I...

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.500
You mustn't move so suddenly! 
You're badly hurt!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.650
<i>Badly... hurt?</i>

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:26.000
<i>That's right... We were...</i>

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.890
Hey!

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.020
Where are the other six?

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.150
Were they saved?!

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.650
Everything is all right.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.530
There are seven, including you.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.170
We brought all of you here.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:52.530
You don't need to worry.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.500
I see... That's good.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.290
You're very kind.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:02.690
It's the duty of a public official 
to be concerned for his citizens.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.540
Forgive me. I haven't introduced myself.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.550
My name is Mikogami Tsukasa.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.040
Would you mind telling me your name?

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.050
My name is Lyrule.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.080
Lyrule-kun, eh?

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.660
Allow me to thank you on behalf of all of us.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.480
I couldn't just ignore 
people who were injured.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.600
It's customary among us
mountain folk to help one another!

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.580
Wait just a moment.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.280
Here you go.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:37.030
It's a stew made with goat's milk.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:39.400
It's delicious!

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.040
Here, open wide.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:44.490
I feel like a child again.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.530
I'm sorry.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.850
It seems I don't quite have 
the strength to eat yet.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:02.640
You'll never get any better 
if you don't eat some meat.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:34.550
If I do that... you can eat it... right?

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:38.850
<i>I suppose it would be in 
bad faith to refuse now...</i>

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:39.940
Thank you.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:43.820
Is it all right if I take advantage 
of your kindness for now?

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:45.560
Yes, of course!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.100
Lyrule!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.120
Is it true that one of the people
we found unconscious is awake now?

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:02.620
Oh, dear. Did I interrupt something?

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:07.000
N-Not at all! 
That wasn't what it looked like!

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.030
It was... a sort of first aid treatment...

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:10.300
<i>Is that the native attire of this place?</i>

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.660
Sure, sure.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.420
Oh, right.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.200
I'm Winona.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.950
I live in this village, like Lyrule here.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:17.930
Nice to meet you!

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.630
My name is Mikogami Tsukasa.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:23.740
It seems my friends and I
owe a great deal to you.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:27.420
Please allow me to thank you properly later,
when I'm back in my own country.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.730
You sound so mature.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.940
You look like you're around 
my son's age, though...

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.580
What? You have a child close to my age?

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.200
You look far too young for that...

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.620
For a kid, you sure know how to flatter!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.820
That tail... Is it actually real?

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.460
Sure it is.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.380
See?

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.420
It's warm...

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.720
<i>There's no doubt. It's a real tail.</i>

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.890
Could it be...

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.840
You've never seen a Byuma before?

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.810
They're all over the place
here in Freyjagard.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.770
<i>Byuma? Freyjagard?</i>

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.960
All seven of you
were wearing unusual clothes.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.770
Could it be that you're from another country?

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:16.920
Uh, yes... I'm from Japan.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.300
Japan?

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:21.320
Never heard of it.

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:23.930
Wh-What are you saying?

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.580
You're both speaking in Japanese right now!

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.610
Huh?

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:29.340
What are you talking about?

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:33.040
All three of us have been
speaking in Altan this whole time.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:38.210
<i>Their eyes, their breathing, 
their speech patterns...</i>

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.800
<i>None of it gives the impression 
that they're lying to me.</i>

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:42.720
<i>Then...</i>

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.520
Freyjagard.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.850
Japan?

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.310
Altan.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.980
<i>What in the world is going on?</i>

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.860
You shouldn't move around yet! 
Your injuries...

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:02.490
Forgive me, but could you take me 
to the site of the plane crash...

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:06.970
I mean, to where you found 
my companions and me?

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:16.820
Four days ago, some sort of large object
flew straight across the sky.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:19.560
Then there was a loud sound,
like a landslide,

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:21.520
so everyone in the entire village ran here.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.570
And then...

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:26.780
We saw that big thing that looks
like a bird skeleton up in flames,

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:28.560
and the seven of you were lying nearby.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.060
<i>Unbelievable...</i>

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.560
<i>There's no way...</i>

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:37.240
<i>we could've survived this.</i>

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.040
<i>Could this mean...</i>

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:50.740
Wow! You don't often see a dragon that big!

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:54.560
Indeed. We should offer
a prayer for your recovery.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.600
It seems I have no choice but to accept it.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.460
What do you mean?

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.970
It appears that we...

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:15.000
have arrived in a different world from ours.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.260
Now, then...

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:33.770
A toast to our seven visitors' full recovery!

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.050
Cheers!

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.390
Cheers!

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:45.480
I still can't believe you kids 
are humans from another world.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.990
That was a real shocker.

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:50.530
You can say that again, Mayor Ulga!

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.240
I'd say we were more shocked than you guys.

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:55.750
Imagine waking up and seeing stuff like <i>that</i>.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.500
Let go!

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:01.050
Then Tsukasa starts talking about
being in another world...

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.800
How are you all faring?

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:07.590
Have you grown accustomed 
to life in our village yet?

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:12.080
Yes, after living here for a month,
we're quite used to it.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.490
Right, Aoi-san?

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:15.100
Indeed.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.250
Of course, there is still one...

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:20.600
...who's having some trouble
accepting reality.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.980
There sure is.

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:24.890
Impossible! Impossible! Impossible!

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.810
This has to be a bad dream! A nightmare!

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:28.420
Yeah! It's just a magic trick!

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:30.400
Or a prank! Either way, it's impossible!

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:33.240
Impossible! Impossible! Impossi—

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:35.240
We're gonna...

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:37.250
...eat you up!

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.250
No! Animal ears! Tails!

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:41.920
No!

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.600
Now, children, you mustn't tease our guests.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:46.340
Run for it!

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:47.760
Honestly...

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:54.220
Anyway, so you all really come 
from a world with no Byuma?

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:56.970
Hey, what's this "Byuma" thing?

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:58.850
Well, um...

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:01.730
Byuma are people like those in this village,

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:05.580
who have animal-like features and, 
in many cases, great strength.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:09.600
People like the seven of you
are known as "Hyuma."

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.360
Though it is very rare,

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:14.610
some Hyuma have the ability 
to use a power called "magic."

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.220
Wow, cool!

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.870
So there's magic here, too!

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:21.790
I see.

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:24.730
That does seem to be 
the most likely explanation

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:27.080
for this unrealistic situation 
we've found ourselves in.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:31.050
We should do some research 
on this world's magic.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:32.280
Agreed!

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:34.390
Sorry for the wait!

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:36.760
I brought steamed potatoes!

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:37.920
Aw, man...

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.390
Potatoes again?

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.810
I'm sick of potatoes.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:44.960
They're a little different today.

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:46.770
They are?

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:47.970
Right, Tsukasa?

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:48.570
Yes.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:51.570
Take some of this... and do this.

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:54.070
What'd you put on it?

00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:56.840
Something Tsukasa made for us.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:57.830
Try it.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.480
It's good!

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.030
So much better than salt!

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:07.670
Way better!

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:09.760
Have one too, Lyrule-kun.

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:11.170
O-Okay...

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:18.200
It's tart, yet mellow! 
I've never had anything like it!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.430
This is the captivating condiment 
that conquered our world...

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:25.440
Mayonnaise.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:33.190
This stuff's delicious!

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:36.200
Would you like another, Mayor Ulga?

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.700
Oh, right, by the way...

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:46.130
Hearing about your situation
reminded me of something.

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:47.560
It did?

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:48.210
Yeah.

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:51.960
There's a story about seven heroes 
who came from another world.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:56.720
I'd like to hear this story in detail.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.550
Well, I don't know the whole story, but...

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:04.200
A long time ago, seven heroes 
appeared from another world

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:07.560
and saved a land that had been
under the control of an evil dragon.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:09.730
It's a fairy tale, really.

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:12.230
Seven heroes who came...

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.740
...from another world?

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.450
That's stupid!

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:21.950
You seriously believe that crap
about them being from another world?

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.500
You even threw this big feast for them!

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:26.970
Imagine how I feel as the village treasurer!

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:29.960
What's the problem? It's a happy occasion.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.090
We can't afford...

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.890
to keep seven useless mouths fed!

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:37.050
Elch.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:39.030
That's enough.

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:41.810
No Elm man should ever say such petty things.

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:47.760
A-Anyway, if your wounds are healed, 
then get out of our village already!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:51.800
I'm sorry about my son.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:52.600
It's all right.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:56.070
We're grateful for all that
Elm Village has done.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:15:59.700
Now...

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:03.820
I'd like to hold a meeting to discuss
how we're going to deal with

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.200
the bizarre situation we are in.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:10.660
Broadly speaking, there are 
three things we need to address.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.210
The first is gathering information 
about this world.

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:18.890
What kind of country Freyjagard is, 
what kinds of laws they have...

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:21.220
And the magic, too!

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:26.470
The second, obviously, is looking for
a way back to our own world.

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:30.200
Our only clue is that story 
about the seven heroes, right?

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:37.650
I'm sure we can look into this while 
gathering information on this world.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:38.990
Agreed.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:38.990
Nin, nin!

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.480
And the third,

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:44.010
and possibly our most 
pressing issue right now,

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:46.740
is rebuilding this village's finances.

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:48.850
I have no objections.

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:51.750
We must to repay our debt to them in full!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.800
These are our three goals.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:57.910
I would like us to consider
each one of them top priority.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.840
Sure.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.840
Nin, nin!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.840
Okay...

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.840
Got it!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.840
Understood.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.840
It shall be done!

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:06.220
I modified all of our cell phones
to work in this world.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.380
Fantastic.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:11.060
Thank you, Ringo-kun.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.380
A-Also...

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.400
I went back to check out the crash site,

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:20.490
and the miniature nuclear reactor
I made was unharmed.

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:23.760
Then we should have
all the power we need for a while.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:24.990
Yeah.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:30.200
<i>One other thing you should bear in mind!</i>

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:34.500
<i>The plane crashed right beside
a beary large deposit of bauxite ore!</i>

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:35.820
Oh?

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:39.890
I want to use that bauxite 
to produce aluminum.

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:42.240
Do we have what we need to refine it?

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.510
The blueprint is already done in my head.

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:46.510
I can finish it in three days.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.280
<i>But with only the bear minimum 
of scrapped plane parts,</i>

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.770
<i>we don't have enough materials!</i>

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:53.770
Understood. We'll ask our merchant for help.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:55.760
Who are you people?!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:56.980
<i>Bear?</i>

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:02.830
Merchant, what's going on here?

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.610
Soldiers on patrol, apparently.

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:09.120
This village doesn't have any meat
or booze to spare you people!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.330
It all goes to our lord!

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.120
Now, don't cry, woman.

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:16.790
I, Schede the Great,
 Imperial Knight of Freyjagard,

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:21.760
am offering protection to you ladies
while your men are away.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:22.650
What?!

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:23.840
We only ask

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:28.480
for a little bit of hospitality in return...

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:31.600
Who the hell are you?!

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:36.880
Soldiers, as much as I appreciate 
your generous offer,

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.390
I must ask you to leave.

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:39.690
Tsu-Tsukasa...

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:43.450
Listen, punk! An affront 
to me, an Imperial Knight,

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:45.700
is an affront to the Freyjagard Empire,

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:49.410
as well as an affront to 
the great Emperor himself!

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:51.370
Boys!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:52.460
Sir!

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:55.370
Show this fool...

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.890
what happens to insolent punks!

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.340
What?!

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.760
Nin, nin!

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:05.260
Indeed.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:07.760
Do you still wish to continue?

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:10.810
You bastard!

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:21.060
Make no mistake. You are but a parasite
leeching off the system.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:22.480
If you value your life,

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:25.240
then get out of here... right now.

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:29.660
You'll pay for this!

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.750
You guys... are really strong...

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:37.830
Was that wise? They may be thugs, 
but they're still soldiers.

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:42.200
If the feudal lord hears about this,
there'll be trouble.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.800
No need to worry about that.

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:50.490
I've already sent out an insurance policy.

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:53.150
Those little brats!

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:56.310
I'll report them to the lord, 
and they'll all be dead meat!

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:58.480
I'm afraid I can't let that comment slide.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.500
Wh-What?!

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:08.990
My name is...

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:11.120
Prince Akatsuki!

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:15.120
I am the great magician 
who protects Elm Village!

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.530
H-He's floating?!

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:20.500
L-Levitation is supposed to be an art
known only to special imperial mages!

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:23.920
What is such a mage doing in
a worthless village like that?!

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:26.630
I owe a debt to those villagers.

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:29.060
And to repay that debt,

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:32.160
I think I'll start by taking your lives.

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:33.600
Perhaps...

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:37.180
like this?

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.440
W-We won't tell! 
We won't tell the lord anything!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.720
I swear! Honest!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.580
Please don't kill me!

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:46.810
Good.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:51.560
In that case, I'll let you 
keep your lives this time.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:56.180
But if you ever break your promise...

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:58.250
You know what'll happen, right?

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:08.090
Good work, Akatsuki.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:10.340
Now...

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.800
Keeping this incident in mind,

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:16.570
I think each of us should do work 
that suits our individual abilities.

00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:17.600
Right.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:21.590
Good. So, once again...

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:25.960
I'm sure you all have your concerns
about this impossibly unrealistic situation

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.900
that we've been thrust into.

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:33.060
I mean, we don't have any idea
how to get back home yet.

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:36.080
There's nothing we can do about that now.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:38.330
But I want you all to remember this.

00:21:38.720 --> 00:21:41.280
The impossible, the unthinkable, 
and the unmanageable

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:46.340
are all things that we have overcome 
countless times to get to where we are.

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:51.630
We have seven people here now
who were called "high school prodigies."

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:55.470
That means that nothing 
should be impossible for us.

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:59.320
So, well... let's just take it nice and easy.

00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:02.230
If we were to give it our all,

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:08.280
we could end up ruining this world.
